        "text": "Page: A. J. Watson. Sentence: Rodger Ward won 18 races driving Watson cars.\nPage: Rodger Ward. Sentence: Rodger M. Ward (January 10, 1921 – July 5, 2004) was a WWII P-38 aviator in the United States Air Force, and an American race driver with 26 victories in top echelon open-wheel racing in North America, two Indianapolis 500 victories, and two USAC National Championships, who conceived the classic tri-oval design and layout of Pocono International Raceway, modeled after his three favorite signature turns, at Trenton, Indianapolis and Milwaukee.\nPage: 1962 USAC Championship Car season. Sentence: The USAC National Champion and Indianapolis 500 winner was Rodger Ward.",
